#4406
Beginning of Scrooge Street~
This lane is known for the main character in the story "A Christmas Carol"
by  Charles Dickens.  The character Scrooge had a change of heart after
being visited by 3 different spirits.  The other streets in the town also 
follow the script.  The city's townspeople have not scrimped at all, when 
it came to the city's design.  The streets are paved with red and white brick,
kinda of in a candy-cane design.  The buildings that lead off this road are also
painted in the same motif as the guardshack outside the gates.  You hear
the faint sounds of haggling and bargaining nearby.~
