E
couch chair ottoman~
A beautiful piece of workmanship, the ebony marvel looks both
dignified and comfortable, this is the place Baddie sits when she is
at her most pensive.  As night falls you can almost imagine BadHabit,
and her sister GoodMood sitting here with their friends discussing
adventures past, and adventures yet to come.  As you sit there
silently, thinking, voices start to sound, and images start to form as
if the room itself is remembering a cheery night.~
E
images room~
As you look around you see BadHabit in her favorite chair, GoodMood
providing a small feast of appetizers, sitting in among the many chairs
you can see Gooddie's husband Jamon, and many of their friends.  As a
small storm starts to brew, a fire lights in the fireplace, without your
help.  As light floods into the corners of the room, the vision fades, and
you are suprised to see a door leading south. As you peer into the next
room, you see what appear to be BadHabit's private chambers.~
S
#4449
The  Retreat~
The first thing you notice upon entering this room is a large, and
plain looking bed, as you take a seat on it to rest your weary bones
it moves out from under you, as if flowing away from your body.
As you look out the small windows you see a winter wonderland beyond them,
and as the beauty of the softly falling snow overwhelms you, you begin to
understand why Baddie finds so much peace here.~
44 8 0
D0
Badhabit's house~
~
0 -1 4448
E
bed~
As you inspect it more closely you are astounded to find that it is
actually made of the skin of an impossibly large buffalo, which is
then filled with water, and sealed.  This water bed is truly a
marvel, not having been seen before in the Realms.  Next to the odd
bed is a small table with a scroll, and plume where it is believed
that Baddie writes her deepest and most personal thoughts.~  
E
plume scroll~
You are tempted to delve into her private scroll, and yet, the power
of her presence lingering around you forbids you, and you cannot resist.
So strong are Baddie's feelings for what she has written that her will
for privacy thwarts even the boldest intruder.~  
